  "acceptance_id": "pocky_syringe3_push_back_v1",
  "notes": "Headless syringe3 push-back PASS/FAIL, run with the housing clamped (options syringe3_two_cycle_clamped.toml): after a 2 s settle the pull actuator ramps 0 to -30 N over 1 s (the handle pushed back), holds -30 N for 1 s, releases for 0.5 s and holds 1 s. The slider legs must stop on the backstop clips. Check mapping: (1) slider_not_back_<phase> is relative_translation of slider in the housing frame along x from the initial state, max_over_phase, lower -0.0005 m: the slider never goes more than 0.5 mm behind home (the clips stand 0.05 mm behind the legs); upper 0.001 m is only a sanity bound (no forward motion while pushed). There is no joint-position-over-phase check kind; the slider body's x in the housing frame is slider_x, as both frames are identity at stroke 0. (2) plate_in_slot_<phase> is the same translation with lower = -(plate_rest_x - rear_x) = -0.0064 m: the plate face stays in front of the rear wall's outer face, so the plate never leaves the slot. (3) slider_home_hold is return_displacement on slider_x at the end of hold, max 1 mm: the spring brings it home after the push. (4) push_effort_bound is effort_bound on pull, max 40 N (PULL_MAX_EFFORT_N; the scenario commands -30 N). (5) Housing pose and signed world-z drop use the two-cycle S0 thresholds (0.2 mm, 0.2 deg, +-0.1 mm), max_over_phase, for push, push_hold, release and hold. (6) penetration_bound 0.2 mm, as the two-cycle file. The three packets of the options file are loaded, as in the two-cycle run, so the stack's weight is on packet 1 as in use; no packet event is checked, as the plate moves away from them. With a free housing MuJoCo filters the housing-slider contact and the slide joint's 0.5 mm guard is the stop instead, so this acceptance is meant for the clamped housing. Expected outcome is not asserted before the run.",
